# Line endings are the same on every OS, whatever core.autocrlf says. Text is checked out with LF, so the
# test fixtures, the model-quality corpus and the PTX kernels a Windows checkout builds from are byte for
# byte the ones a Linux checkout builds from. Batch files are checked out with CRLF: cmd.exe misreads
# labels in a batch file with LF line ends.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
